/image?url=%2Fmedia%2F%DB%B1%DB%B3%DB%B4%DB%B3%DB%B3%DB%B8-scaled-1.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2F%DB%B1%DB%B3%DB%B4%DB%B3%DB%B3%DB%B8-scaled-1.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2F%DB%B1%DB%B3%DB%B4%DB%B3%DB%B3%DB%B8-scaled-1.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2F%DB%B1%DB%B3%DB%B4%DB%B3%DB%B3%DB%B8-scaled-1.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2F%DB%B1%DB%B3%DB%B4%DB%B3%DB%B3%DB%B8-scaled-1.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2F%DB%B1%DB%B3%DB%B4%DB%B3%DB%B3%DB%B8-scaled-1.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w\" src=\"/_next/image?url=%2Fmedia%2F%DB%B1%DB%B3%DB%B4%DB%B3%DB%B3%DB%B8-scaled-1.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75\"/></div><div class=\"prose-blog mt-8\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2>Images of Naqsh-e Jahan Square and the Ali Qapu Palace in <a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/invest/\" rel=\"noopener\">Isfahan</a>– Isfahan</h2>\n<h5>In these photos, you can see the large Naqsh-e Jahan Square of Isfahan</h5>\n<h5>In Naqsh-e Jahan Square's historic bazaar, the Ali Qapu Palace (west side), Sheikh Lotfollah Mosque (east side), and the Shah Mosque are located in the southern part</h5>\n<h5>This square was previously used for polo, but over time its use has changed</h5>\n<h5>There are numerous historic sections in this square, each containing a sea of art</h5>\n<h5>The beautiful tile work in the mosque captivates every viewer and also earns the appreciation of foreign tourists</h5>\n<h5>The paintings that are still visible in the <strong>Ali Qapu Palace</strong> and despite the restorations, have still retained some of their beauty</h5>\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/tj-header-builder/%d9%87%d8%af%d8%b1-%d8%ae%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%87-04-%d8%b1%d9%88%d8%b4%d9%86/logo-secondary/\" rel=\"noopener\">src=\"/media/logo-secondary.png\"</a>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n<h4>I took these pictures a few years ago at <a href=\"https://mehrdad.ir/%d8%a8%d8%b1%da%af%d8%b2%d8%a7%d8%b1%db%8c-%d8%b1%d9%88%d9